  "id": "diffusion-model",
  "term": "diffusion model",
  "definition": "A diffusion model, here the Drift Diffusion Model, is a way of analyzing decision-making that aims to reveal the cognitive processes behind a choice rather than only the final behavior. It can be used to study how people weigh options such as immediate versus delayed outcomes in different contexts like gains and losses.",
